# Shroud (CR 702.18) is hexproof's stricter sibling: nobody may target the creature, its own controller included.
#
# Bot1 plays a Sylvan Safekeeper and a Guerrilla Gorilla. Bot2 aims a Lightning Bolt at the Gorilla; Bot1 answers by
# sacrificing a Forest to give it shroud. The Gorilla is no longer a legal target when the Bolt resolves, so the Bolt
# is countered by the rules (CR 608.2b) and the Gorilla lives with no damage on it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Sylvan Safekeeper
Forest
Guerrilla Gorilla
13 Forest

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
14 Mountain

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sylvan Safekeeper.Cast

[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play

[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Guerrilla Gorilla.Cast

[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Guerrilla Gorilla)

# The cost is a land, not mana, so this works with both Forests tapped.
Bot1.Battlefield.Sylvan Safekeeper.Activate(Guerrilla Gorilla)
Bot1.Choose(Forest)
? Stack = Sylvan Safekeeper; Lightning Bolt

[T5 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Sylvan Safekeeper; Guerrilla Gorilla
Bot1.Graveyard = Forest
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
